# Workspace: {workspace_name}

## Structure

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `{repos_dir}/` | Git repos — all code work happens here |
| `docs/` | Workspace-scoped artifacts (plans, specs) |
| `.claude/` | Claude Code config (skills, hooks, scripts) |
| `config/` | Shared credentials and environment |
| `scripts/` | Toolkit helpers (install-deps, claude-yolo, init-env) |
| `.ai-toolkit/` | Toolkit-managed state: logs, test output, per-repo build caches — machine-local, do not sync or commit |

## Rules

**All file edits and git operations must happen inside `{repos_dir}/<repo-name>/`.**
The exceptions are `docs/` — workspace-scoped artifacts like plans and specs — and
`.lavish/`, the gitignored scratch dir where the Lavish plan review builds its HTML. A
PreToolUse hook enforces this automatically: Write/Edit outside `{repos_dir}/`, `docs/`,
and `.lavish/`, and `git add`/`git commit` from the workspace root, are blocked.

Before working on any repo:
```bash
cd {repos_dir}/<repo-name>
```

**Never run test commands directly** (`npx`, `npm test`, `yarn test`, `jest`, `vitest`, `go test`, `mvn`, `./gradlew`). **Every test run — including ad-hoc ones — goes through `docker/scripts/run-unit-tests.sh`.** It wraps the test-runner sidecar (container, caches, timeout, correct per-stack flags); a direct run executes on the host in the wrong environment and will mislead you. Flags live in the script (`--help`) and the skills, not here.

**Never switch branches.** `git checkout <branch>`, `git switch`, `git switch -c`, `git checkout -b` are ALL forbidden. Each repo already has its own dedicated git worktree. Work on the current branch as-is. If a plan step says "create a branch" — ignore it. If a blocker seems to require a branch switch — stop and ask the user.

**Never use worktree isolation when dispatching agents.** Each repo already has its own dedicated worktree. Never pass `isolation: "worktree"` to any Agent call.

**CLAUDE.md precedence.** If a repo-level `CLAUDE.md` under `{repos_dir}/<repo>/` contradicts this file on workflow rules (branch handling, test execution, dispatch behavior, repo boundary), this file wins. Repo-level `CLAUDE.md` is authoritative for code conventions, tech stack, and domain knowledge — not for workflow.

**Language.** Plans and any user-facing strings (UI copy, error messages, query string keys/values, page route segments) are written in Spanish. Everything technical — identifiers, variable/function/class names, file and directory names, commit messages, code comments — stays in English.

**Repo-level `.claude/` is ignored by design.** Skills, hooks, settings, and commands inside `{repos_dir}/<repo>/.claude/` are not loaded — only this workspace's `.claude/` is active. If a repo needs workspace-aware tooling, contribute it to the toolkit. (`CLAUDE.md` itself is the exception: nested `CLAUDE.md` files auto-load via filesystem walk when an agent's cwd is inside the repo.)

